      // reduction, FInvRMS[t], FNormalized segment and output segment are
      // token-owned, so disjoint token ranges are race-free. The per-token
      // reduction pins the chunk axis to tokens (a depth split would need a
      // cross-chunk combine the single-shot chunk model does not provide), so
      // seq=1 decode gets work count 1 - acceptable for an O(Depth)/token
      // layer. Reads x from pass-stable FPrevLayer.FOutput DIRECTLY - unlike
      // the old Compute() there is no whole-volume identity copy. Also the
      // serial kernel: Compute() calls ComputeRange(0, NumTokens-1).
      // Coded by Claude (AI).
