      // different operand shapes than the forward pass, so they MUST NOT reuse
      // the forward FDotCL: the conv forward prepares FDotCL ONCE in EnableOpenCL,
      // and any (re)prepare - PrepareForCompute or ReallocateBuffersIfRequired -
      // overwrites FNumAs/FNumBs/FSize, which would clobber that once-only forward
      // state and break the next ComputeOpenCL. The two backward GEMMs share this
      // instance via the grow-only ReallocateBuffersIfRequired (safe: each re-uploads
      // its operands, so the reused buffers never carry stale data). Coded by Claude (AI).
