  // Depth-contiguous per-CHANNEL mean / inverse-standard-deviation reduction of a
  // (SizeX,SizeY,Depth) volume: for every channel d independently the mean and
  // inv-std are taken over that channel's SizeX*SizeY spatial map. Each (x,y)
  // position owns a depth-CONTIGUOUS run, so the two reduction passes accumulate
  // as depth-aligned vector ops (TVolume.Add for the per-channel sum, then a
  // centered TVolume.MulAdd self-product for the variance) into the two
  // Depth-length scratch buffers -- never a stride-Depth scalar column gather.
  // OutMean and OutInvStd are Depth-length result vectors; SumScratch and
  // SumSqScratch are caller-owned Depth-length working buffers (so this shared
  // helper allocates nothing). The variance is the mean-subtracted form
  // sum((x-mean)^2)/N, matching the scalar GroupNorm/InstanceNorm reduction
  // exactly. Used by TNNetAdaIN (content half) and TNNetGroupNorm's
  // one-channel-per-group (instance-norm) fast path. Coded by Claude (AI).
  procedure NeuralPerChannelMeanInvStd(V: TNNetVolume;
    OutMean, OutInvStd, SumScratch, SumSqScratch: TNNetVolume;
    Eps: TNeuralFloat);

